      <section id="career-decision-student-guide" class="career-decision-student-guide" aria-labelledby="career-decision-student-guide-title" hidden>
        <div class="career-decision-student-guide-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">A simple way to use this page</p><h3 id="career-decision-student-guide-title">Choose, try, review</h3></div><span class="scope-note">You do not need to decide your whole future today.</span></div>
        <div class="career-decision-journey"><article><b>1</b><div><strong>Choose a career option</strong><span>Read the ordinary work and pick the route that interests you most.</span></div></article><article><b>2</b><div><strong>Try one small task</strong><span>Use a project, conversation, or observation to see how it feels in real life.</span></div></article><article><b>3</b><div><strong>Record what you learn</strong><span>Keep it, change it, or add a secondary option after you have useful evidence.</span></div></article></div>
      </section>
      <section id="career-decision-checklist" class="career-decision-checklist" aria-labelledby="career-decision-checklist-title">
        <div class="career-decision-checklist-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">A simple way to decide</p><h3 id="career-decision-checklist-title">Answer four practical questions</h3></div><span class="scope-note">You do not need a perfect answer today.</span></div>
        <ol>
          <li><strong>Do I understand the ordinary work?</strong><span>Read the daily tasks, not only the job title.</span></li>
          <li><strong>Can I reach it from my current stage?</strong><span>Check the usual course, training, or entry route.</span></li>
          <li><strong>What small test will I complete?</strong><span>Choose one task, conversation, or observation that creates evidence.</span></li>
          <li><strong>What would change my mind?</strong><span>Write down the evidence that would strengthen or challenge this career option.</span></li>
