  <dialog id="help-dialog" class="workspace-dialog help-dialog" aria-labelledby="help-dialog-title">
    <form method="dialog" class="dialog-form">
      <header><div><p class="eyebrow">Workspace guide</p><h2 id="help-dialog-title">How to use this workspace</h2></div><button class="icon-button" type="button" data-close-dialog="help-dialog" aria-label="Close help" title="Close help"><X size={18} /></button></header>
      <div class="dialog-body help-dialog-body">
        <section><h3>Start with the next useful thing</h3><p>Read <strong>Needs attention</strong> on Overview, open the linked record, make one concrete update, and agree the next practical step. You can leave a field blank when you do not know the answer yet.</p></section>
        <section><h3>What the main words mean</h3><dl class="help-definition-list"><div><dt>Primary career option</dt><dd>A career or route the student wants to explore seriously. A plan can include more than one.</dd></div><div><dt>Secondary career option</dt><dd>A useful alternative the student wants to keep open or test later.</dd></div><div><dt>Current ability</dt><dd>What the student can demonstrate today without guessing. Choose the closest level; it is a starting point, not a permanent judgement.</dd></div><div><dt>Evidence</dt><dd>A practical work sample, project, course result, experience, or feedback that shows what the student can do.</dd></div><div><dt>Coach feedback</dt><dd>A specific observation about the work, followed by the next way to practise or improve.</dd></div><div><dt>Satisfaction scales</dt><dd>Coach satisfaction records confidence in the demonstrated progress. Student satisfaction records whether the plan feels useful and clear to the student.</dd></div><div><dt>Cohort</dt><dd>The shared coaching group for a student. Community posts, group commitments, useful links, and guidance can be linked to it.</dd></div></dl></section>
        <section><h3>If something is missing</h3><p>Refresh once. If the record is still missing, check that the student is active and in your scope. An Admin can check account approval, branch assignment, and password setup in <strong>People & access</strong>.</p></section>
        <div class="notice secure"><ShieldCheck size={17} aria-hidden="true" /><span>Private staff notes stay with coaching staff. Only guidance deliberately marked for the student appears in their dashboard.</span></div>
      </div>
      <footer><button class="primary-button" type="submit">Got it</button></footer>
    </form>
  </dialog>

   <dialog id="account-dialog" class="workspace-dialog" aria-labelledby="account-dialog-title">
